<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Acceptance Criteria — Increment 3" id="ac-increment-3">
    <mxGraphModel dx="0" dy="0" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="10540" pageHeight="900" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
<mxCell id="inc3-manage-animation-resource-catalogs-2" value="Manage Animation Resource Catalogs" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="20" width="2250" height="505" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-fx-resource-catalog-fxrepo-data-3" value="Load FX Resource Catalog (FxRepo.data)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="125.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-fx-resource-catalog-fxrepo-data-ac1-4" value="1. WHEN the application starts and `FxRepo.data` is present in the COH Data Directory THEN the FX Resource Catalog is loaded into memory with all FX Resource entries from that file AND the catalog reports a loaded state, enabling the resource picker in the ability editor" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-fx-resource-catalog-fxrepo-data-ac2-5" value="2. WHEN the FX Resource Catalog is loaded THEN each FX Resource entry is accessible by name and COH FX identifier for browsing and assignment" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-fx-resource-catalog-fxrepo-data-ac3-6" value="3. WHEN `FxRepo.data` is missing or unreadable at startup THEN the application falls through to the seed-from-embedded-CSV path BUT the FX Resource Catalog is not reported as loaded from file; the embedded seed path must complete before the catalog is considered ready" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="274" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-fx-resource-catalog-fxrepo-data-ac4-7" value="4. WHEN a resource-picker interaction or element-save operation attempts to use the FX Resource Catalog before it has finished loading THEN the system rejects or blocks that operation BUT no crash or silent failure occurs; the user sees an indication that the catalog is not yet ready" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="370" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-movement-resource-catalog-moverepo-data-8" value="Load Movement Resource Catalog (MoveRepo.data)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="445.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-movement-resource-catalog-moverepo-data-ac1-9" value="1. WHEN the application starts and `MoveRepo.data` is present in the COH Data Directory THEN the Movement Resource Catalog is loaded into memory with all Movement Resource entries AND the catalog reports a loaded state, enabling the resource picker for movement elements" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-movement-resource-catalog-moverepo-data-ac2-10" value="2. WHEN the Movement Resource Catalog is loaded THEN each Movement Resource entry is accessible by name and COH movement identifier" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-movement-resource-catalog-moverepo-data-ac3-11" value="3. WHEN `MoveRepo.data` is missing at startup THEN the application falls through to the embedded-CSV seed path for movement resources BUT no movement-related resource-picker or element-save proceeds until the seed completes" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="274" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-movement-resource-catalog-moverepo-data-ac4-12" value="4. WHEN the Movement Resource Catalog has loaded from a prior session file THEN the in-memory collection matches the persisted entries without re-reading the file mid-session" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="356" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-sound-resource-catalog-soundrepo-data-13" value="Load Sound Resource Catalog (SoundRepo.data)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="765.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-sound-resource-catalog-soundrepo-data-ac1-14" value="1. WHEN the application starts and `SoundRepo.data` is present in the COH Data Directory THEN the Sound Resource Catalog is loaded into memory with all Sound Resource entries AND the catalog reports a loaded state, enabling the resource picker for sound elements" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-sound-resource-catalog-soundrepo-data-ac2-15" value="2. WHEN the Sound Resource Catalog is loaded THEN each Sound Resource entry is accessible by name and COH audio identifier" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="206" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-sound-resource-catalog-soundrepo-data-ac3-16" value="3. WHEN `SoundRepo.data` is missing at startup THEN the application falls through to the embedded-CSV seed path for sound resources BUT no sound-related resource-picker or element-save proceeds until the seed completes" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="266" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-sound-resource-catalog-soundrepo-data-ac4-17" value="4. WHEN the three catalog load sequences complete (FX, movement, sound) in sequence THEN all resource pickers in the ability editor are enabled and populated AND the ability editor is not blocked by pending catalog load operations" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="348" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-seed-resource-catalogs-from-embedded-csv-on-first-run-18" value="Seed Resource Catalogs from Embedded CSV on First Run" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1085.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-seed-resource-catalogs-from-embedded-csv-on-first-run-ac1-19" value="1. WHEN the application starts and no `FxRepo.data` is found in the COH Data Directory THEN the FX Resource Catalog is seeded from the Embedded CSV for FX resources AND the resulting data is written to `FxRepo.data` in the COH Data Directory for future sessions" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="995" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-seed-resource-catalogs-from-embedded-csv-on-first-run-ac2-20" value="2. WHEN the application starts and no `MoveRepo.data` or `SoundRepo.data` is found THEN the corresponding Resource Catalogs are seeded from their respective Embedded CSVs AND each resulting data file is written to disk before the catalog is marked loaded" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="995" y="206" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-seed-resource-catalogs-from-embedded-csv-on-first-run-ac3-21" value="3. WHEN a catalog data file already exists on disk THEN the embedded CSV is not read for that catalog type BUT the file-based load path is used exclusively" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="995" y="302" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-seed-resource-catalogs-from-embedded-csv-on-first-run-ac4-22" value="4. WHEN the embedded CSV for a catalog type is absent or unreadable in the assembly THEN the application reports the catalog as unavailable BUT it does not crash; the remaining catalogs that can be seeded are still loaded" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="995" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-seed-resource-catalogs-from-embedded-csv-on-first-run-ac5-23" value="5. WHEN all three catalogs have been seeded and written on first run THEN subsequent application restarts load from the written data files without seeding again" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="995" y="452" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-fx-resources-for-ability-authoring-24" value="Browse FX Resources for Ability Authoring" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1405.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-fx-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac1-25" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Add FX in the Ability Editor element list THEN a resource picker opens showing all FX Resource entries from the FX Resource Catalog AND each entry displays its name and COH FX identifier" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1315" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-fx-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac2-26" value="2. WHEN the GM selects a FX Resource in the picker and confirms THEN a new FX Element is added to the ability&apos;s element list with that resource reference AND the element appears at the bottom of the ordered list" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1315" y="192" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-fx-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac3-27" value="3. WHEN the GM dismisses the picker without selecting a resource THEN no element is added to the ability BUT the ability&apos;s existing element list is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1315" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-fx-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac4-28" value="4. WHEN the FX Resource Catalog contains no entries (empty catalog) THEN the resource picker displays an empty state message BUT the Add FX action remains accessible without error" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1315" y="342" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-movement-resources-for-ability-authoring-29" value="Browse Movement Resources for Ability Authoring" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1725.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-movement-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac1-30" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Add MOV in the Ability Editor element list THEN a resource picker opens showing all Movement Resource entries from the Movement Resource Catalog" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1635" y="110" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-movement-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac2-31" value="2. WHEN the GM selects a Movement Resource and confirms THEN a new Movement Element is added to the ability&apos;s element list with that resource reference AND the element appears at the bottom of the ordered list" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1635" y="178" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-movement-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac3-32" value="3. WHEN the GM dismisses the picker without selecting THEN no element is added BUT the existing element list is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1635" y="260" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-movement-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac4-33" value="4. WHEN the Movement Resource Catalog is not yet loaded THEN the Add MOV action is disabled or the picker shows a not-ready state BUT no crash or data corruption occurs" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1635" y="320" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-sound-resources-for-ability-authoring-34" value="Browse Sound Resources for Ability Authoring" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2045.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-sound-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac1-35" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Add Sound in the Ability Editor element list THEN a resource picker opens showing all Sound Resource entries from the Sound Resource Catalog" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1955" y="110" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-sound-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac2-36" value="2. WHEN the GM selects a Sound Resource and confirms THEN a new Sound Element is added to the ability&apos;s element list with that resource reference AND the element appears at the bottom of the ordered list" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1955" y="178" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-sound-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac3-37" value="3. WHEN the GM dismisses the picker without selecting THEN no element is added BUT the existing element list is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1955" y="260" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-browse-sound-resources-for-ability-authoring-ac4-38" value="4. WHEN the Sound Resource Catalog is empty THEN the picker displays an empty state BUT the Add Sound action remains accessible and does not error" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1955" y="320" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-configure-abilities-39" value="Configure Abilities" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2300" y="20" width="1930" height="469" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-create-animated-ability-40" value="Create Animated Ability" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2405.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-create-animated-ability-ac1-41" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Create in the ability list on the Crowd Manager — Abilities screen THEN a new Animated Ability is added to the selected character&apos;s Abilities Option Group with a default name and empty element list AND the new ability appears in the ability list" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2315" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-create-animated-ability-ac2-42" value="2. WHEN the new Animated Ability is created THEN its activation key is unset, persistence flag is off, attack flag is off, and default flag is off AND it has zero Animation Elements" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2315" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-create-animated-ability-ac3-43" value="3. WHEN the GM attempts to create a second Animated Ability with the same name as an existing one on the same character THEN the system rejects the creation AND an inline error is displayed indicating the name must be unique BUT no ability is added" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2315" y="274" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-create-animated-ability-ac4-44" value="4. WHEN no character is selected in the crowd tree THEN the Create action in the ability list is disabled BUT the ability list remains visible in its empty state" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2315" y="356" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-edit-animated-ability-45" value="Edit Animated Ability" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2725.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-edit-animated-ability-ac1-46" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Edit on an Animated Ability in the ability list THEN the Ability Editor opens pre-populated with the ability&apos;s current name, Activation Key, persistence flag, and attack flag AND the element list shows all existing Animation Elements in their current order" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2635" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-edit-animated-ability-ac2-47" value="2. WHEN the GM modifies fields and saves THEN the Animated Ability is updated with the new values AND the ability list in Crowd Manager — Abilities reflects the updated name and key" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2635" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-edit-animated-ability-ac3-48" value="3. WHEN the GM cancels without saving THEN the Animated Ability retains its previous values unchanged AND the Ability Editor closes, returning to Crowd Manager — Abilities" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2635" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-edit-animated-ability-ac4-49" value="4. WHEN the GM attempts to save with a name that duplicates another ability on the same character THEN the save is rejected with an inline validation error BUT the Ability Editor remains open so the GM can correct the name" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2635" y="342" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-edit-animated-ability-ac5-50" value="5. WHEN the GM saves successfully THEN the Ability Editor closes and the updated ability is selected in the ability list" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2635" y="424" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-delete-animated-ability-51" value="Delete Animated Ability" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3045.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-delete-animated-ability-ac1-52" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Delete on an Animated Ability in the ability list THEN the ability and all its Animation Elements are permanently removed from the character&apos;s Abilities Option Group AND the ability no longer appears in the ability list" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2955" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-delete-animated-ability-ac2-53" value="2. WHEN the deleted ability was the Default Ability for the character THEN no ability carries the default flag after deletion BUT other abilities on the character are unaffected" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2955" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-delete-animated-ability-ac3-54" value="3. WHEN the deleted ability is currently executing (playing) THEN execution is stopped before the ability is removed BUT no error is raised; the stop completes cleanly before deletion" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2955" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-delete-animated-ability-ac4-55" value="4. WHEN a Reference Element in another ability refers to the deleted ability by name THEN the Reference Element remains in the referencing ability&apos;s element list AND when the referencing ability is played, the missing reference resolves to a no-op BUT no cascade deletion of elements in other abilities occurs" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2955" y="328" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-set-ability-activation-key-56" value="Set Ability Activation Key" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3365.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-set-ability-activation-key-ac1-57" value="1. WHEN the GM uses the set-key action on an Animated Ability in the ability list THEN the Activation Key is updated on that ability and displayed in the key column AND the Keyboard Hook will now dispatch this ability when the new key is pressed" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3275" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-set-ability-activation-key-ac2-58" value="2. WHEN the GM assigns an Activation Key already used by another ability on the same character THEN the system rejects the assignment with a validation message BUT the ability retains its previous key value" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3275" y="192" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-set-ability-activation-key-ac3-59" value="3. WHEN the GM clears the Activation Key (assigns no key) THEN the ability is no longer keyboard-dispatchable AND the key column in the ability list displays empty" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3275" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-set-ability-activation-key-ac4-60" value="4. WHEN the ability&apos;s Activation Key is set and the Keyboard Hook is active THEN pressing the key while the character is active dispatches the ability per Ability Dispatch rules" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3275" y="342" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-toggle-ability-persistence-61" value="Toggle Ability Persistence" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3685.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-toggle-ability-persistence-ac1-62" value="1. WHEN the GM toggles persistence on an Animated Ability that is currently non-persistent THEN the persistence flag is set and the persistent indicator appears in the ability list row AND the ability will replay automatically on each subsequent Identity load" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3595" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-toggle-ability-persistence-ac2-63" value="2. WHEN the GM toggles persistence off on a Persistent Ability THEN the persistence flag is cleared and the indicator is removed AND the ability no longer replays on identity load" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3595" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-toggle-ability-persistence-ac3-64" value="3. WHEN a Persistent Ability is active and the character&apos;s Active Identity changes THEN the persistent ability is stopped before the identity switch completes AND the persistent ability is restarted after the new identity has finished loading" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3595" y="274" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-toggle-ability-persistence-ac4-65" value="4. WHEN a Persistent Ability is deactivated (persistence cleared while active) THEN the Load Persistent Costume on Deactivation behavior applies: the persistent-FX costume variant is reloaded onto the Spawned NPC BUT no persistent replay occurs on subsequent identity loads after deactivation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3595" y="356" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-set-default-ability-for-character-66" value="Set Default Ability for Character" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4005.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-set-default-ability-for-character-ac1-67" value="1. WHEN the GM uses set-default on an Animated Ability in the ability list THEN that ability receives the default flag and the default indicator is shown in its row AND any previously designated Default Ability on the same character has its default flag cleared" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3915" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-set-default-ability-for-character-ac2-68" value="2. WHEN a character with a Default Ability is spawned THEN the designated Default Ability is automatically played on the Spawned NPC AND no manual play action is needed for this initial activation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3915" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-set-default-ability-for-character-ac3-69" value="3. WHEN the Default Ability is removed from the character THEN no ability carries the default flag after removal AND subsequent spawns do not auto-play any ability" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3915" y="288" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-set-default-ability-for-character-ac4-70" value="4. WHEN the GM clears the default designation (set-default toggled off) THEN no ability on the character has the default flag AND the ability list shows no default indicator" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3915" y="356" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-compose-animation-elements-71" value="Compose Animation Elements" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4260" y="20" width="2570" height="505" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-movement-element-to-ability-72" value="Add Movement Element to Ability" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4365.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-movement-element-to-ability-ac1-73" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Add MOV in the Ability Editor element list and selects a Movement Resource THEN a new Movement Element is added to the ability&apos;s element list at the bottom position AND the element displays its type (MOV), resource name, and order position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4275" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-movement-element-to-ability-ac2-74" value="2. WHEN the Movement Element is executed during ability play THEN the referenced COH movement command is applied to the target Spawned NPC AND execution continues to the next element in the sequence" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4275" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-movement-element-to-ability-ac3-75" value="3. WHEN the Movement Resource referenced by the element is not found in the Movement Resource Catalog at execution time THEN the element produces a silent no-op BUT subsequent elements continue to execute; the ability does not halt" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4275" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-movement-element-to-ability-ac4-76" value="4. WHEN the GM reorders the new Movement Element via drag-drop THEN its order position updates and all affected elements&apos; positions shift accordingly AND the new order is persisted when the ability is saved" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4275" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-sound-element-to-ability-77" value="Add Sound Element to Ability" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4685.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-sound-element-to-ability-ac1-78" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Add Sound in the Ability Editor element list and selects a Sound Resource THEN a new Sound Element is added to the ability&apos;s element list at the bottom position AND the element displays its type (Sound), resource name, and order position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4595" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-sound-element-to-ability-ac2-79" value="2. WHEN the Sound Element is executed during ability play THEN the referenced COH audio identifier is played AND execution continues to the next element" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4595" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-sound-element-to-ability-ac3-80" value="3. WHEN the Sound Resource is not found at execution time THEN the element produces a silent no-op BUT subsequent elements continue" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4595" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-sound-element-to-ability-ac4-81" value="4. WHEN multiple Sound Elements are present in the ability THEN each plays in turn according to the element order position AND no simultaneous collision between sound plays is managed at this increment" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4595" y="342" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-fx-element-to-ability-82" value="Add FX Element to Ability" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5005.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-fx-element-to-ability-ac1-83" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Add FX in the Ability Editor element list and selects a FX Resource THEN a new FX Element is added to the ability&apos;s element list at the bottom position AND the element displays its type (FX), resource name, and order position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4915" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-fx-element-to-ability-ac2-84" value="2. WHEN the FX Element is executed during ability play THEN the COH FX command for the referenced resource is issued on the target Spawned NPC AND execution continues to the next element" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4915" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-fx-element-to-ability-ac3-85" value="3. WHEN the FX Resource referenced by the element does not resolve at execution time THEN the element produces a silent no-op BUT subsequent elements continue; the ability does not halt" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4915" y="260" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-fx-element-to-ability-ac4-86" value="4. WHEN the Spawned NPC is not present in the game world when the FX Element executes THEN the FX command produces a no-op BUT no error is raised and subsequent elements continue" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4915" y="342" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-reference-element-to-another-ability-87" value="Add Reference Element to Another Ability" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5325.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-reference-element-to-another-ability-ac1-88" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Add Reference in the Ability Editor element list and names a target ability on the same character THEN a new Reference Element is added showing the referenced ability name and order position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5235" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-reference-element-to-another-ability-ac2-89" value="2. WHEN the Reference Element is executed during ability play THEN the referenced ability&apos;s full element list is executed inline at that point in the parent sequence AND execution returns to the parent sequence after the referenced ability completes" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5235" y="192" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-reference-element-to-another-ability-ac3-90" value="3. WHEN the GM attempts to create a Reference Element that references the owning ability itself (self-reference) THEN the system rejects the reference with a validation message BUT the element is not added" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5235" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-reference-element-to-another-ability-ac4-91" value="4. WHEN the referenced ability does not exist on the character at execution time THEN the Reference Element produces a silent no-op AND subsequent elements in the parent ability continue" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5235" y="370" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-reference-element-to-another-ability-ac5-92" value="5. WHEN a circular reference chain would be created (A → B → A) THEN the second reference that closes the circle is rejected at save time BUT the existing valid reference structure is preserved" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5235" y="438" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-sequence-element-and-or-93" value="Add Sequence Element (And/Or)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5645.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-sequence-element-and-or-ac1-94" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Add Sequence in the Ability Editor element list and chooses And or Or THEN a new Sequence Element of the specified type is added to the element list AND the element displays its type (And or Or), order position, and zero child elements initially" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5555" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-sequence-element-and-or-ac2-95" value="2. WHEN the Sequence Element is executed with type And THEN every child Animation Element is executed in ascending order position AND execution returns to the parent sequence after all children complete" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5555" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-sequence-element-and-or-ac3-96" value="3. WHEN the Sequence Element is executed with type Or THEN exactly one child Animation Element is selected at random and executed AND all other sibling children are skipped; execution returns to the parent sequence after the chosen child completes" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5555" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-sequence-element-and-or-ac4-97" value="4. WHEN the Sequence Element contains no child elements at execution time THEN the element produces a no-op BUT execution of the parent sequence continues uninterrupted" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5555" y="370" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-sequence-element-and-or-ac5-98" value="5. WHEN the GM changes the execution type (And → Or or Or → And) on an existing Sequence Element THEN the type change is saved with the ability AND child elements are unaffected" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5555" y="438" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-pause-element-99" value="Add Pause Element" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5965.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-pause-element-ac1-100" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Add Pause in the Ability Editor element list and configures a duration THEN a new Pause Element is added to the element list with the specified duration and order position AND the element displays its type (Pause) and configured duration value" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5875" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-pause-element-ac2-101" value="2. WHEN the Pause Element is executed during ability play THEN progression to the next element is blocked for the configured duration AND after the pause completes, the next element begins execution normally" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5875" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-pause-element-ac3-102" value="3. WHEN the pause duration is set to zero THEN the Pause Element is a no-op delay and execution continues immediately to the next element" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5875" y="288" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-pause-element-ac4-103" value="4. WHEN the ability is stopped mid-execution while a Pause Element is active THEN the pause timer is cancelled and the stop completes immediately BUT no partial timing effect is applied to subsequent plays" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5875" y="356" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-load-identity-element-104" value="Add Load-Identity Element" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6285.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-load-identity-element-ac1-105" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Add Identity in the Ability Editor element list and names a target identity on the same character THEN a new Load-Identity Element is added showing the target identity name and order position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6195" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-load-identity-element-ac2-106" value="2. WHEN the Load-Identity Element is executed during ability play THEN the named identity is set as the Active Identity on the character AND subsequent elements in the sequence execute after the identity switch completes" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6195" y="192" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-load-identity-element-ac3-107" value="3. WHEN the target identity does not exist on the character at execution time THEN the element produces a no-op BUT subsequent elements continue; the ability does not halt" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6195" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-load-identity-element-ac4-108" value="4. WHEN the GM saves an ability containing a Load-Identity Element referencing a valid identity THEN the element is saved with the identity name AND if the identity is later renamed or removed, the element retains the original name (no cascade update)" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6195" y="342" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-reorder-animation-elements-via-drag-drop-109" value="Reorder Animation Elements via Drag-Drop" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6605.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-reorder-animation-elements-via-drag-drop-ac1-110" value="1. WHEN the GM drag-drops an Animation Element from one position to another in the element list THEN the element moves to the target position AND all elements between the old and new positions shift by one position to accommodate" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6515" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-reorder-animation-elements-via-drag-drop-ac2-111" value="2. WHEN the GM drops the element in the same position it started THEN the element list is unchanged AND no save is triggered unless other changes were made" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6515" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-reorder-animation-elements-via-drag-drop-ac3-112" value="3. WHEN the GM saves after a reorder THEN the new element order is persisted on the Animated Ability AND subsequent play executes elements in the updated order" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6515" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-reorder-animation-elements-via-drag-drop-ac4-113" value="4. WHEN the GM cancels after a reorder (without saving) THEN the element order reverts to the state before the drag-drop AND the persisted ability retains its previous order" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6515" y="328" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-reorder-animation-elements-via-drag-drop-ac5-114" value="5. WHEN multiple reorder actions are performed before save THEN only the final order at save time is persisted" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6515" y="396" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-play-abilities-in-game-115" value="Play Abilities in Game" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6860" y="20" width="1610" height="437" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-play-animated-ability-on-character-116" value="Play Animated Ability on Character" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6965.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-play-animated-ability-on-character-ac1-117" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Play on an Animated Ability in the ability list and the character is spawned THEN the ability begins executing its Animation Elements in order on the target Spawned NPC AND an active ability indicator is shown on the ability row" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6875" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-play-animated-ability-on-character-ac2-118" value="2. WHEN the ability&apos;s Animation Elements all complete THEN the ability stops and the active indicator is cleared from the row" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6875" y="206" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-play-animated-ability-on-character-ac3-119" value="3. WHEN the GM selects Play on an ability whose character is not currently spawned THEN the play is blocked with a visible indication BUT no game command is issued and no error is raised" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6875" y="266" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-play-animated-ability-on-character-ac4-120" value="4. WHEN another ability on the same character is already executing THEN the currently executing ability is stopped before the new ability begins AND the new ability&apos;s execution starts from its first element" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6875" y="334" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-stop-active-ability-121" value="Stop Active Ability" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7285.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-stop-active-ability-ac1-122" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Stop on an Animated Ability that is currently executing THEN execution is halted immediately; the current element is abandoned AND the active ability indicator is cleared from the row" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7195" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-stop-active-ability-ac2-123" value="2. WHEN the GM selects Stop and no ability is currently executing on the character THEN the stop action is a no-op BUT no error is raised" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7195" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-stop-active-ability-ac3-124" value="3. WHEN a Persistent Ability is stopped via the stop action THEN the persistence flag is not cleared; the ability retains its persistence designation AND it will replay on the next identity load as expected" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7195" y="260" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-stop-active-ability-ac4-125" value="4. WHEN the ability is stopped mid-pause-element THEN the pause timer is cancelled immediately AND no subsequent elements execute" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7195" y="342" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-execute-animation-sequence-and-sequential-or-random-126" value="Execute Animation Sequence (And: sequential, Or: random)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7605.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-execute-animation-sequence-and-sequential-or-random-ac1-127" value="1. WHEN a Sequence Element with type And executes THEN every child Animation Element is executed one after another in ascending order AND each child completes before the next begins" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7515" y="110" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-execute-animation-sequence-and-sequential-or-random-ac2-128" value="2. WHEN a Sequence Element with type Or executes THEN exactly one child Animation Element is selected at random (uniform distribution) AND only that child executes; all other siblings are skipped" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7515" y="178" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-execute-animation-sequence-and-sequential-or-random-ac3-129" value="3. WHEN an Or Sequence Element contains exactly one child THEN that single child always executes (deterministic result) AND no random selection error occurs" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7515" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-execute-animation-sequence-and-sequential-or-random-ac4-130" value="4. WHEN a Sequence Element (And or Or) is nested inside another Sequence Element THEN the inner sequence executes according to its own type before the outer sequence continues AND nesting to any depth is supported" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7515" y="328" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-maintain-persistent-ability-across-identity-changes-131" value="Maintain Persistent Ability across Identity Changes" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7925.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-maintain-persistent-ability-across-identity-changes-ac1-132" value="1. WHEN a character&apos;s Active Identity is changed while a Persistent Ability is executing THEN the Persistent Ability is stopped before the identity switch begins" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7835" y="110" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-maintain-persistent-ability-across-identity-changes-ac2-133" value="2. WHEN the new Active Identity has finished loading on the Spawned NPC THEN the Persistent Ability is automatically replayed from its first element AND the active indicator returns on the ability row" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7835" y="178" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-maintain-persistent-ability-across-identity-changes-ac3-134" value="3. WHEN a character has multiple Persistent Abilities THEN all of them are stopped before the identity switch and all replay after AND each restarts independently" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7835" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-maintain-persistent-ability-across-identity-changes-ac4-135" value="4. WHEN the character is despawned while a Persistent Ability is active THEN the persistent ability is stopped BUT the persistence flag is not cleared; the ability will still replay on the next spawn-and-identity-load" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7835" y="328" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-persistent-costume-on-deactivation-136" value="Load Persistent Costume on Deactivation" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8245.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-persistent-costume-on-deactivation-ac1-137" value="1. WHEN a Persistent Ability is deactivated (persistence flag cleared while the ability is active) THEN the Persistent-FX Costume Variant is loaded onto the Spawned NPC via the Load Costume Command AND the visual state of the character in the game world reflects the persistent-FX appearance after deactivation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8155" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-persistent-costume-on-deactivation-ac2-138" value="2. WHEN the deactivation occurs and the character is not spawned THEN the Load Costume Command is not issued BUT the persistence flag is still cleared on the ability" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8155" y="220" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-persistent-costume-on-deactivation-ac3-139" value="3. WHEN a character has multiple Persistent Abilities and one is deactivated THEN only the costume variant relevant to that ability is reloaded AND remaining active Persistent Abilities are unaffected" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8155" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-load-persistent-costume-on-deactivation-ac4-140" value="4. WHEN the Persistent-FX Costume Variant file does not exist at deactivation time THEN the Load Costume Command is not issued AND the character retains its current in-game appearance without error" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8155" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-manage-default-abilities-141" value="Manage Default Abilities" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8500" y="20" width="650" height="437" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-default-abilities-to-character-142" value="Add Default Abilities to Character" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8605.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-default-abilities-to-character-ac1-143" value="1. WHEN the Add Default Abilities operation is applied to a character THEN all 20 named abilities from the Default Ability Set are added to the character&apos;s Abilities Option Group AND each ability appears in the ability list with its standard name" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8515" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-default-abilities-to-character-ac2-144" value="2. WHEN the default abilities are added THEN each is created with no Activation Key, persistence off, attack flag reflecting its combat nature, and no default designation AND their element lists are pre-populated with the standard element configuration for each named ability" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8515" y="192" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-default-abilities-to-character-ac3-145" value="3. WHEN Add Default Abilities is applied to a character that already has one or more of the standard abilities by name THEN duplicate names are not added AND only the abilities whose names are not already present are created" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8515" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-add-default-abilities-to-character-ac4-146" value="4. WHEN Add Default Abilities is applied to a new character with an empty Abilities Option Group THEN all 20 abilities are added without conflict AND the ability list shows exactly 20 rows after the operation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8515" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-refresh-ability-activation-eligibility-147" value="Refresh Ability Activation Eligibility" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8925.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-refresh-ability-activation-eligibility-ac1-148" value="1. WHEN the eligibility conditions for an Animated Ability change (e.g., character spawned/despawned, ability execution starts/stops, activation key assigned/cleared) THEN the Ability Activation Eligibility is refreshed and reflects the updated state" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8835" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-refresh-ability-activation-eligibility-ac2-149" value="2. WHEN an ability has no Activation Key set THEN its Ability Activation Eligibility is ineligible AND the Keyboard Hook does not dispatch it" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8835" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-refresh-ability-activation-eligibility-ac3-150" value="3. WHEN an ability is currently executing THEN its Ability Activation Eligibility is ineligible for re-trigger BUT the ability continues executing; no interruption occurs" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8835" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-refresh-ability-activation-eligibility-ac4-151" value="4. WHEN the character is not spawned THEN all of its abilities report ineligible Ability Activation Eligibility AND no keyboard dispatch fires for any of them" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8835" y="342" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-handle-global-keyboard-shortcuts-152" value="Handle Global Keyboard Shortcuts" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9180" y="20" width="1290" height="519" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-install-low-level-keyboard-hook-153" value="Install Low-Level Keyboard Hook" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9285.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-install-low-level-keyboard-hook-ac1-154" value="1. WHEN the application starts and the hook installation is requested THEN the Keyboard Hook is installed as a low-level Windows keyboard hook AND subsequent key events are intercepted by the application for routing evaluation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9195" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-install-low-level-keyboard-hook-ac2-155" value="2. WHEN the hook is successfully installed THEN the Keyboard Hook is in the installed state and Ability Dispatch can fire on matching key presses" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9195" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-install-low-level-keyboard-hook-ac3-156" value="3. WHEN the hook installation fails (e.g., insufficient OS permissions) THEN the application reports the failure AND keyboard-triggered Ability Dispatch is disabled for the session BUT direct play actions in the ability list remain fully functional" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9195" y="260" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-install-low-level-keyboard-hook-ac4-157" value="4. WHEN the application shuts down THEN the Keyboard Hook is uninstalled cleanly, releasing the OS hook handle BUT no key events are intercepted after uninstall" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9195" y="356" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-route-key-events-when-game-window-is-focused-158" value="Route Key Events when Game Window is Focused" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9605.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-route-key-events-when-game-window-is-focused-ac1-159" value="1. WHEN the COH game window is the foreground window and the GM presses a key THEN the Keyboard Hook evaluates Key Routing against the Active Character&apos;s abilities" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9515" y="110" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-route-key-events-when-game-window-is-focused-ac2-160" value="2. WHEN Key Routing finds an Animated Ability whose Activation Key matches the pressed key and eligibility permits THEN Ability Dispatch fires and the ability begins executing on the character" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9515" y="178" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-route-key-events-when-game-window-is-focused-ac3-161" value="3. WHEN no ability on the Active Character has an Activation Key matching the pressed key THEN the key event is passed through to the game without dispatch BUT no error or notification is generated" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9515" y="246" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-route-key-events-when-game-window-is-focused-ac4-162" value="4. WHEN the COH game window loses foreground focus mid-session THEN subsequent key presses no longer trigger game-window routing AND dispatch only fires again when the game window regains foreground focus" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9515" y="328" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-route-key-events-when-application-window-is-focused-163" value="Route Key Events when Application Window is Focused" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9925.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-route-key-events-when-application-window-is-focused-ac1-164" value="1. WHEN the HVT application window is the foreground window and the GM presses a key THEN the Keyboard Hook evaluates Key Routing using the same logic as Game Window Focus AND Ability Dispatch fires on a match with eligible activation eligibility" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9835" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-route-key-events-when-application-window-is-focused-ac2-165" value="2. WHEN neither the COH game window nor the HVT application window is the foreground window THEN key events are not routed and Ability Dispatch does not fire BUT the Keyboard Hook remains installed and continues to intercept events for future focus events" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9835" y="192" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-route-key-events-when-application-window-is-focused-ac3-166" value="3. WHEN the application window is focused and the GM presses a key that matches an ability THEN the dispatch fires and the ability executes on the active character&apos;s Spawned NPC AND the active indicator appears on the ability row in the Crowd Manager — Abilities screen" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9835" y="288" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-route-key-events-when-application-window-is-focused-ac4-167" value="4. WHEN the application window transitions from focused to unfocused THEN the routing for application-window focus is suspended immediately for subsequent key presses" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9835" y="384" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-dispatch-ability-activation-keys-to-characters-168" value="Dispatch Ability Activation Keys to Characters" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10245.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-dispatch-ability-activation-keys-to-characters-ac1-169" value="1. WHEN a key press is received through Key Routing and the Active Character has an Animated Ability with a matching Activation Key THEN Ability Dispatch retrieves that ability and initiates execution of its element list on the character&apos;s Spawned NPC" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10155" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-dispatch-ability-activation-keys-to-characters-ac2-170" value="2. WHEN Ability Activation Eligibility for the matched ability is ineligible at dispatch time THEN the dispatch is suppressed; the ability does not execute BUT the key event is still consumed (not passed to the game for other uses)" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10155" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-dispatch-ability-activation-keys-to-characters-ac3-171" value="3. WHEN there is no Active Character at dispatch time THEN the key event is passed through without dispatch BUT no error is raised" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10155" y="288" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-dispatch-ability-activation-keys-to-characters-ac4-172" value="4. WHEN the Active Character has multiple abilities and more than one shares the pressed key (an invariant violation) THEN the system dispatches the first eligible match and logs the ambiguity AND the invariant violation should be surfaced as a validation warning in the ability list" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10155" y="356" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc3-dispatch-ability-activation-keys-to-characters-ac5-173" value="5. WHEN dispatch fires successfully and the ability completes THEN the active indicator is cleared on the ability row AND the Ability Activation Eligibility is refreshed to eligible for the next key press" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10155" y="452" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>